- [compactContextIntentValue, context-intent-contracts.ts:571–585](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/9de83bcd9f46c1966c4bdb20639f0b6067b4687b/src/sdk/context-intent-contracts.ts#L571-L585), blob `5e3a185678b60b4b7f6435be469c620f9cce2526`

## Minimal public-SDK reproduction

Run in an isolated consumer where the package is already installed; the example only constructs in-memory results.

```js
import assert from "node:assert/strict";
import { applyReadOutputDimensions } from "@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk/core";

const title = "a".repeat(239) + "😀" + "z".repeat(5000);
const input = () => ({
  items: [{ id: "pm-synthetic-1", title, status: "open" }],
  count: 1,
  total: 1,
});

assert.equal(title.isWellFormed(), true);

assert.throws(
  () => applyReadOutputDimensions(
    "list",
    { outputFormat: "toon", outputBudget: 1000 },
    input(),
  ),
  {
    name: "TypeError",
    message: "Cannot encode string value containing an unpaired surrogate U+D83D at index 239",
  },
);

const json = applyReadOutputDimensions(
  "list",
  { outputFormat: "json", outputBudget: 1000 },
  input(),
);
assert.equal(json.read_output.strings_compacted, true);
assert.equal(json.items[0].title.isWellFormed(), false);

const unbounded = applyReadOutputDimensions(
  "list",
  { outputFormat: "toon", outputBudget: "unbounded" },
  input(),
);
assert.equal(unbounded.items[0].title, title);
```

A separate installed-module check of `attachContextIntentReceipt("list", { for: "triage", tokenBudget: 1000 }, input())` produces `recursive_budget_compaction` with the same invalid string; rendering that result as TOON throws too.

Controls: putting the emoji at index **238** or **240** does not split the pair in either exact-source helper. Uncompacted input and the unbounded public-SDK case preserve the full valid text.

## Impact and expected behavior

Bounded reads containing ordinary valid emoji/other astral characters at this boundary can fail during output rendering or token estimation. JSON consumers instead receive a malformed truncated string. This evidence concerns emitted projections; it does not demonstrate persisted tracker corruption or data loss, and it does not attribute any particular production incident.

Both compaction paths should share a Unicode-safe bounded-prefix primitive. Keep the encoder's malformed-input rejection. Avoid manufacturing lone surrogates, substituting replacement characters, or weakening output-budget accounting.

Acceptance coverage should include:
- Both ordinary output-budget and context-intent compaction, including nested records/arrays
- Valid astral characters immediately before, across, and after the cutoff, with no lone surrogate or replacement character in retained output
- TOON and JSON parity, plus original-input immutability and unbounded-read preservation
- The existing preserved-string exceptions and exact rendered-budget/receipt checks
- CLI/SDK/MCP coverage of the shared boundary, while distinguishing source tests from installed-release acceptance

## Ownership / duplicate check

All-status issue/PR searches for surrogate, unpaired, Unicode, emoji, 240, the error text, and the compaction helpers found no matching output-compaction defect. [PR #1279](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1279) / [pm-cimph7](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8/.agents/pm/issues/pm-cimph7.toon) concern the already-closed shell-completion Unicode boundary, not these output helpers.

This belongs under the existing SDK read-output/context-intent lineage: [pm-5t33or](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8/.agents/pm/features/pm-5t33or.toon) (open output-budget feature), [pm-hb7ug8](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8/.agents/pm/features/pm-hb7ug8.toon) and [pm-cxr0jb](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/8aeb18ce546c402abfac43dffdd65908c884a1b8/.agents/pm/features/pm-cxr0jb.toon) (closed foundational features, delivered through #873). The closed cursor/history issues #1371/#1411/#1325 address different contracts.
